    <statement><p>A stone is thrown straight up from the edge of a roof,
 800   feet above the ground, at a speed of 18
feet per second.</p>
<p>A.  Remembering that the acceleration due to gravity
is  -32  feet per second squared, how high is the stone 6
seconds later?  <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/> ft.</p>
<p>B.  At what time does the stone hit the ground? <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0002"/> s.</p>
<p>C.  What is the velocity of the stone when it
hits the ground? <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0003"/> ft/s.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-16\cdot 6^{2}+18\cdot 6+800</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{18+\sqrt{18\cdot 18+64\cdot 800}}{32}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-32\cdot 7.65591+18</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
